  "explanation": {
    "event_selection": "The unified specification uses only task-level search, approach, claim, pickup, drop, and delivery-publication events together with the object, zone, claim, pickup, and delivery observations required to execute one complete color-matched delivery. Low-level movement and obstacle events are omitted because collision_avoidance already protects motion and the objective does not request direct low-level movement control. Release events are omitted because a successful claimant retains its selected object while retrying failed searches, pickups, or drops.",
    "transition_design": "From object_search, repeated search_object actions permit selection of any visible red, green, or blue object. Each visibility observation enters its matching claim-attempt state, where only the corresponding claim event succeeds; received_claim and received_delivered observations abandon an unavailable target. A successful claim immediately enables repeated approach_object actions. Object not-visible observations return to a claimed-object search state, and object-reached observations from either claimed search or approach enable pick_up_object. Pickup confirmation starts the matching zone protocol, while failure retries the claimed object. Repeated search_zone and approach_zone actions are restricted to the matching color, with not-visible observations returning to zone search and reached observations enabling drop_object. Delivery failure retries the matching zone, while confirmation enables only the matching publication event and then reaches delivery_complete. No delivery actions are enabled after delivery_complete, so each controller completes at most one object delivery.",
